The image is highly relevant to the research presented in the PDF. It directly corresponds to Figure 6 in the "Journal of Controlled Release" PDF, which is titled "Nano-11 enhances the expression of CD80 and CD86 on DCs." The PDF states in section 3.4, "Nano-11 activates DCs in vitro," that "Incubation of BMDCs with Nano-11 for two days slightly increased expression of CD40 and induced a marked increase of the expression of CD80 and CD86 (Fig. 6)." The histograms in the image visually confirm these findings, showing the relative expression levels of CD40, CD80, and CD86 on dendritic cells after Nano-11 treatment, thus providing direct evidence for Nano-11's ability to activate dendritic cells by upregulating costimulatory molecules.